WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.630
- I started an internet
trend and this is the story.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.580
This story starts on a lazy Sunday.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.180
I was hanging out in my apartment alone,

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.530
just having a weird day.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.020
Sometimes I like to have weird days,

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.730
and I play Nintendo and I eat stuff

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.290
and I drink beer and it's great.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.520
So this is one of those Sundays

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.950
and I'm scrollin' social media,

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.260
which is my favorite thing to do,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.290
and I notice that there's this
whole conversation going on

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.341
about the way Ariana Grande is dressed

00:00:24.341 --> 00:00:25.870
on this album cover.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:26.780
Some people are saying

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.550
that a women shouldn't
have to dress like that

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.780
because she's a singer.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.240
What does her body have to do with it?

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.120
Other people were saying

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:33.680
that she should dress however she wants.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.900
Even though this album
came out three years ago,

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.980
everyone was dissecting
what she's wearing.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.590
I was staring at this album
cover for like an hour

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.450
for a different reason.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.460
She is seated on the stool in a way

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.350
that didn't make sense to my brain.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.660
It's like one of those
drawings of a staircase

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.590
that goes on forever,
(eerie music)

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.860
it was like an optical illusion.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.620
I didn't understand how
it was physically possible

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.440
that this picture could've been taken.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.480
She's kneeling in this way.

00:01:01.658 --> 00:01:03.800
Even my hands feel
awkward trying to do it,

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.690
but it does look plausible enough

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.380
where maybe she did take the photo.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.330
It wasn't like, oh, this is
an obviously bad Photoshop.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.580
It was driving me fucking crazy.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.260
So, at first, I'm genuinely not thinking

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.240
about social media or the internet,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.000
and I filled up my camera
roll with photos of myself

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.260
kneeling on a stool in front of a mirror

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.170
to try to see if I could do it.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.610
I couldn't, first of all.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:29.430
I fell down multiple times,
I almost broke my arm,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.260
and I'm looking back
through all these photos

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.500
and I'm like, I look
fucking crazy right now,

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.430
but I feel like other people
would be interested in this.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:39.020
I pick a couple photos that
show I'm really struggling,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.600
I also pick ones that
don't clearly show my face

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.330
because it's a little embarrassing.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.230
So I posted it to Twitter.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.180
Then I usually take my
tweets and I screen grab them

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.550
and put them on Instagram.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.450
I hashtag Ariana Grande.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.830
No one really notices
it for a couple hours.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.180
I continue drinking
beer and playing Zelda,

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.200
and then my phone starts blowing up.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.800
I realize it's taken off on Instagram.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.230
If you post it on Instagram,

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:06.680
the most amount of people that usually

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.420
are going to like something
are your followers,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.370
and I didn't have that
many followers at the time.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:13.830
All of a sudden it has
40-something thousand likes.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.020
I'm getting tagged in photos
of people trying it themselves.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:19.580
Now people are going back
to finding me on Twitter,

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.490
posting replies to my original
tweet of them doing it.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.410
I can't understate how quickly

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.840
this thing was just
blowing up my mentions.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.250
My phone was hard to use,
(bomb explodes)

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.940
it was running so slowly.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.910
It was from Instagram and
Twitter just buzz, buzz, buzz.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.250
I started actually getting nervous.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:35.940
I'm like, what if there's
something in the background

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.690
of the photo that people are
just gonna make fun of me for.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.920
What if my job has some
weird deal with Ariana Grande

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.400
that they're like, you blew it!

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.530
When I walk over to my
phone and pick it up

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.420
and see my latest notification,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.764
it said Ariana Grande
replied to your tweet.

00:02:50.764 --> 00:02:51.830
(door slams)

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.650
I'm assuming, at this point,
this is a fan account.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.810
If you look at pop stars like
Taylor Swift or Lady Gaga,

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.780
Ariana Grande, they have
these huge fan accounts,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.320
some of them are verified.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.350
I thought this was one of them.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.200
I opened Twitter,

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.490
I see Ariana Grande actually
quote tweeted my tweet,

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.160
'Next week on MythBusters,'

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.560
and at that point I'm like, fuck.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.200
She is one of the
biggest Twitter accounts.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.500
Young fans are a horrifying force.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.330
If they think that you're going
after a star, you're done.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.010
So I was immediately terrified

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.460
that Ariana Grande interacted with it

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.940
because I was like, okay,
the fans are coming for me.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:28.090
It was like I felt the fuckin' stampede.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.890
Luckily, this was a positive force.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.330
They were all happy about it.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.930
They were all positive
about it, which was great.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:40.080
My Instagram followers grew
like crazy, which is good,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.090
but it's a lot of Ariana Grande fans

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.380
who are gonna be sadly disappointed

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.370
when I post the next selfie.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.420
At this point, things went
from being, let's say,

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.420
blowing up on social media to viral.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.730
I think people throw
around the word viral.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.860
People will say this went viral

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.480
when really it just got shared

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.410
in their local fishing community
Facebook page or something,

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.290
and that's pretty much
everything I have ever posted

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.610
that's done super well.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.720
It's been like, oh yeah,
this corner of the internet

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.170
who loves the movie Hocus
Pocus shared this thing,

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.630
but I wouldn't say it went viral.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:14.730
To me, something actually
going viral means that

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:19.180
your mom's neighbor's
hairdresser knows about it.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.630
I'm getting emails from
Good Morning America,

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:24.060
I got a message from someone at The View.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.550
There's one from Australia,

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.030
there's one from The Netherlands,

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.450
there's an international
television producers

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.450
who were messaging me and emailing me.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.410
So I'm just, honestly, excited by this.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:36.730
It is nerve wracking.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:38.830
When TV shows reached out, I'm thinking,

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.850
use the photos all you
want, talk about it,

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.240
I do not want to be on TV talking about

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.550
how I spent my Sunday in my underwear

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.370
taking pictures of myself
in an Ariana Grande pose.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.010
I just couldn't do it (laughs).

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:53.670
I think the pinnacle of what
I would call this going viral,

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.120
like something actually going viral,

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.880
is my mom texting me saying
she's at the nail salon

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.330
and opened In Touch magazine

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:05.400
and saw a story about the
Ariana Grande stool thing

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.320
that mentioned me.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.210
To me, the watermark of viral is now

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:11.190
if your mom texts you from the nail salon

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.830
that she just read in a magazine
about the thing you made.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.310
There is a lot I learned
from this experience.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.900
It was really nice seeing

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:21.160
that you can make something
that's just earnest,

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.920
just an observation.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.911
It wasn't making fun of Ariana Grande,

00:05:24.911 --> 00:05:27.290
it wasn't making fun of the people

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:28.530
who designed the album cover,

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.490
it wasn't making fun of her fans.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.220
It was just something that, universally,

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.670
was a fun thing to participate in.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.150
I basically ended all of it

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:40.499
by trying the stool challenge
myself for real this time,

00:05:40.499 --> 00:05:45.499
and I just posted a photo
that was me in the stool

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:50.340
as best as I could pose
that said, myth plausible.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:55.340
To this day, I do not
think I've seen one person

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:58.940
successfully pose in the same way she did.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:05:59.970
This happened last year,

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:02.020
but I'm gonna say the challenge lives on.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.330
If you're watching this, try it yourself

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:08.210
and tag me if you think
you can actually do it

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:12.017
because I don't think it's
actually been done so far.

00:06:12.017 --> 00:06:14.850
(classical music)

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:25.135
(door squeaks)

